      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_shifted: insert_after_residue 31 -> 34 on human canonical Q8IV16 (paper numbering: ortholog:mouse, construct species: mouse). Paper (PMID 35229724): \"A vector for S-GPIHBP1 was generated by replacing sequences for GPIHBP1 residues 32 to 48 with sequences for the S-protein tag\". Audit note: Residues 32-48 are mouse GPIHBP1 (PENYNYDDDDDEEEEEE, the knock-in Gpihbp1-S allele; detection antibody 11A12 is anti-mouse); this is a replacement/deletion of the acidic domain, not an insertion. Mouse 31|32 aligns to human 34|35 (EDEDHG|PDDYDE) by BLOSUM62, low-complexity region so +/-2. S-GPIHBP1 reaches the CHO cell surface (PI-PLC releasable) and capillary lumen, but LPL transcytosis is lost and mice are hypertriglyceridemic, i.e. function impaired.] L1 explicitly names residues 32\u201348 as the replaced region, placing the tag junction after residue 31 (E) in canonical UniProt numbering; Python confirms seq[30]='E' and seq[31]='D'. GPIHBP1 is GPI-anchored with no TM helix, so residues 21\u2013184 are entirely extracellular and there is no TM-proximity constraint. The acidic domain (residues 32\u201348) is a disordered, low-complexity stretch well-suited to tag replacement, and L4/L5/L7 confirm the tagged protein reaches the cell surface in both mouse endothelium and transfected CHO cells. Full-length GPI-anchored GPIHBP1 construct in which residues 32\u201348 (the acidic domain including the sulfated tyrosine) were replaced with the 15-aa S-protein tag (KETAAAKFERQHMDS). Expressed in CHO pgsA-745 cells (L6/L7) and knocked into the mouse Gpihbp1 locus by CRISPR/Cas9 (L2/L3). Non-permeabilized immunocytochemistry (L7) and intravascular antibody perfusion of mouse hearts (L4) confirmed tag accessibility on the extracellular/luminal surface.",
